  "quality_notes": [
    "Codex, Opus and legacy Direct each passed 12/12 strict decision probes across the two context sizes. Sonnet passed 6/6 full-frame decision probes. These are narrow format/flag checks, not broad intelligence or executed-work acceptance.",
    "Prepared context was present; models sometimes referred to historical call details and produced long handoff replies. Presence is not proof of perfect relevance, compact acknowledgments or complete retrieval.",
    "Haiku 4.5 plain JSON failed strict parsing in all default-thinking and thinking-off decision samples. Native structured output produced a correct boolean in all three trials but one exposed internal workers and two asked for extra permission. It is not a quality-parity recommendation.",
    "The legacy Direct natural-speech batch had two connection failures. Reinitializing the same configured client yielded three successful rechecks; failures remain included. No root cause or runtime reliability repair is claimed.",
    "Native CLI cost fields are token-price estimates, not evidence of API billing. Authentication was plan sign-in; API credential environment was excluded from native children."
  ],
